   "notes": "John Lewis Downing St front (2008). Stone return at the corner (x 0-3), then a long recessed frontage: ground-floor shop glazing behind slender columns (~4.5 m), above it tall dark-glazed bays with vertical fins/mullions in ~6 m bays (~7 bays) up to ~12.5 m, then a plain buff limestone band to ~18 m, with a set-back top storey under projecting roof blades. Bay count and pitch estimated from oblique views."
